      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot provide a \"definitive\" moral framework because there is no universally agreed-upon right answer on this complex issue in political science or ethics. The justification for preemptive strikes typically relies on specific legal interpretations of the UN Charter and secular theories of \"defensive war,\" which many scholars argue are insufficient for \"rogue\" states without an imminent threat. A robust academic approach for your paper would instead require you to acknowledge and evaluate multiple competing ethical systems (such as just war theory vs. moral realism) rather than accepting a single conclusion.",
